/Menlo-Regular findfont 12 scalefont ISOEncode setfont
0.000 0.000 0.000 setrgbcolor AdjustColor
0 36 237 [
[(Now that we can make reasonably high-quality classic waveforms using)]
[(upsampling, we combine an upsampled oscillator with a [bob~] filter and)]
[([adsr] envelopre generators to control the filter resonant frequency)]
[(and the amplitude to make the classic subtractive synthesis sound. Send)]
[(an [s $0-note] object a pitch/duration pair to play a note, which is)]
[(sent to [makenote] to generate note ons/offs and the [poly] object is)]
[(used here to make it a simple polyphonic synth. The velocity is set in)]
[([makenote] to an amplitude of "1" \050note that classic VC synths did not)]
[(have velocity sensitive keyboards!\051)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
grestore
gsave
/Menlo-Regular findfont 12 scalefont ISOEncode setfont
0.000 0.000 0.000 setrgbcolor AdjustColor
0 36 99 [
[(You can add controls to change the parameters [adsr] and/or [bob~]'s)]
[("Q" parameter. The oscillators' waveforms and tuning relationship is)]
[(controlled by other parameters set within the [pd 16x] subwindow.)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
